1. Strong NCOERs that reflect superior performance and potential in a variety of challenging assignments.
2. Exceeded course standards (Honor Graduate and Commandant’s List).
3. Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
4. Consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities.
5. Consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
6. Demonstrated exceptional duty performance and leadership qualities.
(e) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Tactical/Technical Competence, Teamwork, Decision Making, General Cognitive Ability, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Situational Awareness, Active Listening, and Stress Tolerance', 'd12f22d391bba2dbec3fbbb75476ce241b16fce108a25a3cec12fa23e3fbb79c', 10, 10, '10', 51, null, null, false, null),
  ('cd980628-9e5e-57a0-9ece-5d86e04ce004', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Continue pursuit of associate degree or higher-level civilian education. NCO of the Month/Quarter/Year Boards. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', 'c66bbdffd7a3e7d9c9d196863573a318e51a233cd1c6f42e5fdfbf8702d2f3e1', 10, 10, '10', 52, null, null, false, null),
  ('2bd29143-b562-59be-80d6-c13b2f842794', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Functional training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’ Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), Ship Crane Certifications, Ship Loading and Stowage, ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC), Global Air Transportation Execution Systems-Surface (GATES), and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical Transportation of HAZMAT (CERT). Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Army Career Tracker (ACT) for complete Professional Development Model for 88H.', '131242c4475fd8808027c9fca630e3782f73cc437bc88a260ec46809d555189d', 10, 10, '10', 53, null, null, false, null),
  ('65be40a7-1af5-5ec3-8d47-26aec1cc365a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Drill Sergeant; Recruiter', '7ef27181abd3269696637608e92446900eed251e41faadf7b0a1d2512e7f4427', 10, 10, '10', 54, null, null, false, null),
  ('ce67147b-49a5-5577-9099-7415894c9308', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'In preparation for promotion to SFC, complete ALC. Attend Transportation Deployment/Distribution Senior Leader Course (SLC), if possible. Graduating with honors from SLC should be a goal.', '0a466b6b0457a2e6eafcd410bcff13fd44cad573b7c2fa2c51e24286f300527a', 11, 11, '11', 55, null, null, false, null),
  ('7672b465-2907-5a7f-85fb-03b0512d97dc', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Seek assignments in the Operating Force at company and BN levels focused on continued development and refinement of leadership skills and MOS competency. Seek tough leadership positions and excel in the performance of the duties associated with those positions. Seek to become a transportation functional expert and develop knowledge of how to exploit transportation conveyances of rail, truck, vessel, and air to accomplish the mission. Staff Sergeants should also seek out tough leadership positions such as Platoon Sergeant.', 'bdb7596c4174e0dd74c6417834658ea7ad09164f2b0c58ab25a6e1f0779e57cb', 11, 11, '11', 56, null, null, false, null),
  ('d0ea3e76-a406-506f-9bc1-fc33def0e37c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'The 88H SSG must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Section Chief, Foreman, Assistant Operations Sergeant, Terminal Operations NCO, Load Planner, Operations NCO, Cargo Handler and Cargo Handler NCO. Recommend SSGs obtain 24 months experience in a critical leader development position.', '27902d5764c2356235921955a4b4425069c1ccccbdfdf682bf8f0992f131b2f1', 11, 11, '11', 57, null, null, false, null),
  ('d4d649dd-cce4-53b0-be9d-92760d17ad32', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, Drill Sergeant, , ALC Instructor, Recruiter, and Training Management NCO. Superior performance in these type of positions sets NCOs apart from their peers.', 'e3c74983173ddd018e787af8543ce598d9af49d0104a943d252b578ca497b30b', 11, 11, '11', 58, null, null, false, null),
  ('30d18d71-9ba7-5bfa-9531-a2b7099e1d2e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SSGs for the next higher grade.
1. Most qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions: Section Chief, Foreman, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and show consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC).
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault Course; Airborne Course; Ranger School.
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; be recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions, such as Assistant Operations SGT, Terminal OPS NCO, Load Planner, Operations NCO/SGT, Cargo Handler, Cargo Handler NCO.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, AIT Instructor, ALC Instructor, or Training Management NCO (BOLC, Log Ldr College).
(j) Serve as a Presidential Support Driver or Highway Operations Sergeant (White House Transportation Agency) or serve in a Security Force Assistance BDE (SFAB).
2. Highly qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in a position such as Section Chief or Foreman.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and show consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Assistant Operations SGT, Terminal OPS NCO, Load Planner, Operations NCO/SGT, Cargo Handler, Cargo Handler NCO.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, AIT Instructor, ALC Instructor, or Training Management NCO (BOLC, Log Ldr College).
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Teamwork, Training & Developing Others, Management, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Active Listening, General Communication, Safety & Compliance, and Reasoning.', 'aee1cce87a2c359ec43381bb01ad2fcdf71df42505225a30074dd56212474e4e', 11, 12, '11', 59, null, null, false, null),
  ('eb063408-a85c-5a24-9c17-f0717c9930d7', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Continue pursuing higher-level civilian education opportunities, with a goal of completing an associate degree. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '5ec759dcb05ee5524faaa48ce1b0a45df30386ec8bfc1d2dda7daae62e745ab2', 12, 12, '12', 60, null, null, false, null),
  ('8217cc44-b594-54aa-8e8b-60482246d533', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Additional functional training includes TC-AIMS II, (The Transportation Coordinators’ Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE) and/or Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), Ship Crane Certifications, Ship Loading and Stowage, ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Global Air Transportation Execution Systems-Surface (GATES), and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT) and Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC). Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications, a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Army Career Tracker (ACT) for complete Professional Development Model for 88H. Battle Staff NCO Course (BSNCOC), Support Operations Course (SOC), and Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC).', '6d024047811dfe6126c8d21fce1a88801126f02b9c13613adaffcbda2333774f', 12, 12, '12', 61, null, null, false, null),
  ('bdba5839-5bdc-5a16-8029-f467b02bcce3', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'In addition to the Broadening Assignments listed above, the Army Enlisted Aide Program is an opportunity open to all NCOs to serve on the personal staff of a general/flag officer. It is not recommended for a NCO to serve back-to-back tours in special assignments.', '622f797c8f5aea6968a06a4c00fea511a14c4444e5bcac220599e31b6e97b46b', 12, 12, '12', 62, null, null, false, null),
  ('023b0ade-4d6e-544b-8097-8825d00eb37e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'In preparation for promotion to MSG, complete SLC. Attend Master Leader Course (MLC), if selected. Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education Course I (SEJPME I).', 'e7c418cd6c2daa6f9f0b6f1db2b499e7f1d5e7e664805d7d5e250afd81c32195', 12, 12, '12', 63, null, null, false, null),
  ('a44731ca-59d9-54e9-a0ca-41964a7adf7f', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'SFCs should maintain a good balance of generating and operating force assignments that enhance a Soldier’s experience, knowledge, and career progression. NCOs who have served successfully and frequently in challenging leadership positions are considered more competitive for promotion than those who have not.', 'e11695240e9b66e6e14f188d5c7992a4a97a43678391fef50669c0796cc839b8', 12, 12, '12', 64, null, null, false, null),
  ('94dc05c4-7a22-5e82-81da-0d30c1fa9238', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'The 88H SFC must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Platoon Sergeant, Terminal Operations Sergeant, Detachment Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, Cargo NCO, Cargo Handler, Mobilization Deployment Planning NCOIC. The Platoon Sergeant position is key for successful development within the Sustainment Warfighting Function. Recommended time in this critical position is 24-36 months.', '540df0ed18b77f9dac5170844562ccc7eb7c9512a640bac19f514d655818e906', 12, 13, '12', 65, null, null, false, null),
  ('c1845156-11f8-5c13-b3c7-0450fe9f429a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, Drill Sergeant, SLC Small Group Leader, Recruiter, Inspector General NCO, Training Developer, Senior Capabilities Development NCO, Training with Industry, and Talent Management NCO.', '93462a5fdf55d2041ddbb15ad7903a43ff025ee94170c548c3a6bb87eb4bfcea', 13, 13, '13', 66, null, null, false, null),
  ('223c8ef0-4afb-534b-a5c6-510f92e0806c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SFCs for the next higher grade.
1. Most qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions Platoon Sergeant, Terminal OPS NCOIC, Detachment Sergeant, or a position of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff; Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC- AIMS II (Functional User); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC).
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault; Airborne; Ranger School.
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Terminal Operations Sergeant; Platoon SGT; Operations Sergeant.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant; Recruiter; AIT Instructor, SLC SGL; Talent Management NCO (HRC); Senior Capabilities Development NCO; Training with Industry; Inspector General NCO; Senior Instructor; Training Developer.
(j) Serve as a Presidential Support Driver or Highway Operations Sergeant (White House Transportation Agency) or serve in a Security Force Assistance BDE (SFAB).
2. Highly qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in a position such as Platoon Sergeant; Terminal Operations Sergeant; Detachment Sergeant.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Operations Sergeant, Cargo NCO; Terminal Operations Sergeant; Detachment Sergeant/Training NCO; Cargo Handler, Mobility Deployment Planning NCOIC.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant; Recruiter; AIT Instructor; SLC SGL; Talent Management (HRC); Senior Capabilities Development NCO; Training With Industry; Inspector General NCO; Senior Instructor; Training Developer.
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Management, Multi-Domain Collaboration, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Systems Thinking, Communication, Safety & Compliance, and Stress Tolerance.', '80cee8176727c74a97be999da7be7435d5be86b19a8fb3484853f3d56cb3a08f', 13, 14, '13', 67, null, null, false, null),
  ('c6197f2a-13c9-597a-a18d-be8176db2bb9', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Complete associate degree. The completion of an associate degree conveys initiative and potential. Begin pursuing a bachelor’s degree or other higher-level education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', 'be21889698c9bbb1d53f5bed3774e7dbc99499dcbaa8b018ee35de61ddcef137', 14, 14, '14', 68, null, null, false, null),
  ('9f220508-eb3f-5537-aadc-cf990186210d', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'Additional functional training includes TC-AIMS II, (The Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), Ship Crane Certifications, Ship Loading and Stowage, ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, GATES, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT), UMODPC, BSNCOC, Support Operations Course, and Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC). Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Army Career Tracker (ACT) for complete Professional Development Model for 88H.', '8f79d909d2d8b60c3f02f87b8e45a82e4371ecb9a5c4186457ecdec0b8842fed', 14, 14, '14', 69, null, null, false, null),
  ('102fabde-aa99-57f7-b52b-156b69d30e8e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignment', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'In additions to the Broadening Assignments listed above, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), SARC, Defense Attaché, and Army Enlisted Aide are additional opportunities 88H SFCs can pursue. It is not recommended for a NCO to serve in back-to-back tours in special assignments.', '0a074afd756fe7cad0600b35ec3628f38d6884c7643e873fdf51d88337c4a022', 14, 14, '14', 70, null, null, false, null),
  ('a2e9677a-22de-59d0-b316-94164bc24ff0', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88H', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army career degrees', 'Chapter 4. Military occupational specialty 88H Cargo Specialist', 'See SOCAD Army Degree Program.
(6) Master Sergeant/First Sergeant and Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major. See Chapter 25.', '759197a00164abdc51dd09ca6e9a58940a65a7b90b3d2d462273d846df179e91', 14, 14, '14', 71, null, null, false, null),
  ('c530a84d-f106-56f8-aa34-a113b9ff4e69', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Watercraft Operator Course. Attend Basic Leader Course (BLC), if possible. Obtaining recognition as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Distinguished Leader, Honor Graduate or Commandant’s List in BLC should be a goal. Attend Watercraft Operator Certification Course (Course# 062-F5), no earlier than 24 months after completing 88K AIT but prior to promotion to SGT, to attain MOS certifications required IAW AR 56-9 to serve in 20 level positions.', '02512481669dc8f178de76074b88e011f12bac319776c3068cc13250fa9bbca4', 15, 15, '15', 72, null, null, false, null),
  ('45720b10-bce9-5175-982b-30d293f2ebf1', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'These include positions focused on the functional aspect of the MOS at the company level, which build a strong base of technical expertise in equipment, basic MOS skills and common Soldier tasks. Positions such as Seaman allow the Soldier to gain functional and leadership experience.', 'c0bdc5710ed7a4d9467bb74efa6d881337be33a3704d73485d1837a782a65d62', 15, 15, '15', 73, null, null, false, null),
  ('53731e58-8152-585a-a7c4-7b99f5bd5531', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', '(c) Promotion indicators. Indicators a Soldier has promotion potential include maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards, consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities, and consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
(d) Attributes must reflect: One who is culturally astute, agility, adaptability, and resiliency.', 'a333a222cf7d9f6d48634047eeeb0c108e4e5a11eb78579ab940f17df11ae4a2', 15, 15, '15', 74, null, null, false, null),
  ('3af568ae-ba21-5215-9899-c243776f94e8', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Begin pursuing an associate degree or higher-level civilian education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '22ce38707bac4005d5823c458ff5b7cab6c465432437ddc1116c35164ab540a0', 15, 15, '15', 75, null, null, false, null),
  ('e259c6b3-2c89-53a2-99b1-1e2289d6dd64', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Additional training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Continue certification and licensing to grade IAW requirements outlined in AR 56-9. In addition to skill level certification to grade, other training includes TC-AIMS II, (The Transportation coordinators’ Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT CERT. Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88K on ACT for more information.', '48e5f6b8c9116ab87026b595a32aa34275458946204d4e401baf85b6f9d7b1c6', 15, 15, '15', 76, null, null, false, null),
  ('9224d2c1-c0a1-5e36-aaf6-2e57f3d73661', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'N/A', 'e2f79e5b60330bba4c289962231b6ba2957d0b14e7deb3110417003c79dea635', 15, 15, '15', 77, null, null, false, null),
  ('bcb74d8a-3584-5645-aa50-91b331d0c928', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'In preparation for promotion to SSG, complete BLC. Attend Watercraft Operator Advanced Leader Course (ALC) prior to promotion to SSG to attain 30 level MOS certifications required IAW AR 56-9 to serve in 30 level positions on vessels. Graduating with honors from ALC should be a goal.', 'cf64cad18d432941902031ed17cec0cd88f411b34d7121c97644bcc87aed6b16', 16, 16, '16', 78, null, null, false, null),
  ('34d846a5-98f8-5d46-8d27-725dbc013eeb', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Focus on assignments at the company level that develop leadership skills and enhance technical and tactical skills. Seek assignments that provide an opportunity to serve in a leadership position. NCOs who have served frequently and successfully in challenging positions are considered more competitive and better candidates for promotion.', '8e4d1c17b9b66f8e902bc8d5d417429c853d0fac7ec8a39f838255d47c4500e0', 16, 16, '16', 79, null, null, false, null),
  ('ced96beb-0440-5d62-b26a-eb7cd93ed0f4', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'The 88K SGT must seek out key leadership positions as a Leading Seaman, Coxswain, Marine Safety NCO, Dispatcher, or DSTE Operations.', 'c86b3031917f655f6a27dcd171cb88f38ac300e210691f2f3a0b789f996f0435', 16, 16, '16', 80, null, null, false, null),
  ('2b8ac1c6-411c-5a9c-b4cf-f511469409b8', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', '(d) Promotion Indicators are.
1. Strong NCOERs that reflect superior performance and potential in a variety of challenging assignments.
2. Exceeded course standards (Honor Graduate and Commandant’s List).
3. Maintained high physical fitness and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
4. Consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities.
5. Consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
6. Demonstrated exceptional duty performance and leadership qualities.
(e) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Tactical/Technical Competence, Teamwork, Decision Making, General Cognitive Ability, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Situational Awareness, Safety & Compliance, and General Communication.', '8d425a2734f242c4d89d9d5c7d04509885de492d0ad99dd446a45803b96aa336', 16, 16, '16', 81, null, null, false, null),
  ('c0ffcc65-3801-5153-8406-e13f559bdcec', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Continue pursuit of associate degree or higher-level civilian education. NCO of the Month/Quarter/Year Boards. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', 'c66bbdffd7a3e7d9c9d196863573a318e51a233cd1c6f42e5fdfbf8702d2f3e1', 16, 16, '16', 82, null, null, false, null),
  ('430e0f51-b0e2-5169-8b6a-a045b78ea40e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Additional functional training includes Maritime Radar Observers Course (MROC). Aside from skill level certification to grade, other training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional; however important training includes BSNCOC, and the Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88K on ACT for more information.', '8b67f6f02ea5e510aec1d74357c632d90e59c2e99b536857cf710be052c52090', 16, 16, '16', 83, null, null, false, null),
  ('9ad4dfc7-6bdd-5285-a5a5-4265ef9c5bd6', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Drill Sergeant; Recruiter.', '851f2b6221d0dedcd105001f6dc5da2405c93043234f8d0fe14f2a807b4d88c7', 16, 16, '16', 84, null, null, false, null),
  ('103a48d5-a9cc-55a5-91f1-de99b95b8425', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Attend Watercraft Operator Senior Leader Course (SLC) prior to attain 40 level certifications required IAW AR 56-9 to serve in 40 positions on vessels. Attend Transportation Deployment/Distribution Senior Leader Course (SLC), if possible. Graduating with honors from SLC should be a goal.', '3130f267d6e456a98d7f295c2b085efbc04d2b442439ed59f8118bb8e091ed06', 17, 17, '17', 85, null, null, false, null),
  ('2b10fb7e-1d2c-5405-ae4d-57b6e6778d16', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Seek assignments at company and BN levels focused on continued development and refinement of leadership skills and tactical and technical expertise. Seek out the tough leadership positions, which offer unique opportunities in the areas of leadership and problem solving and excel in duties associated with those positions. These positions.', '38f7c206e6b9f3c28f512f6d99de4dbb9ff1136d9ce1eefef303771c74c36f70', 17, 17, '17', 86, null, null, false, null),
  ('2ef2079a-7c75-5994-9170-04ee67734c7f', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'The 88K SSG must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Section Sergeant, Boatswain, and Watercraft NCO. Recommend SSGs obtain 24 months experience in a critical leader development position.', 'bbc9db68eeb7a44d24419bbad83b89c65d631c573ad11575e0175fcba148ce77', 17, 17, '17', 87, null, null, false, null),
  ('5b0f172f-b883-524e-b033-93c4dde5fc6c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Key opportunities include Drill Sergeant, Recruiter. Superior performance in these type of positions sets NCOs apart from their peers.', '23534cd4c794575514ebad3bdc484e4e21a4fb3c3053bbf052d8d74868d1e311', 17, 17, '17', 88, null, null, false, null),
  ('35d0aaaa-63aa-510c-90cd-388c4f8e2500', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SSGs for the next higher grade.
1. Most qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions Section Sergeant, Boatswain, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC- AIMS II (Functional User); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course.;
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault Course; Airborne Course; or Ranger School.
(f) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(g) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Watercraft NCO, Boatswain, Section Sergeant.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant, Recruiter.
2. Highly qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in a position such as Section Sergeant, Boatswain.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Marine Standardization Examiner (MSE); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Watercraft NCO.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant; Recruiter.
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Tactical/Technical Competence, Training and Developing Others, Decision Making, General Cognitive Ability, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Situational Awareness, Safety & Compliance, and General Communication.', '9033c682a11437af509803880a3a66bc8c399bca125944ed4e86c7b42a1b0d7e', 17, 18, '17', 89, null, null, false, null),
  ('00e71ab0-08b1-5eb1-a300-474e68b442f7', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Continue pursuing higher-level civilian education opportunities, with a goal of completing an associate degree. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '5ec759dcb05ee5524faaa48ce1b0a45df30386ec8bfc1d2dda7daae62e745ab2', 18, 18, '18', 90, null, null, false, null),
  ('06fe2045-f76d-5ba1-b748-0f64f1d36ee6', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'K30 Certification, K40 Certification Bridge RM, Global Maritime Distress and Safety System, and Maritime Radar Observers Course (MROC). Aside from skill level certification to grade, other training includes TC-AIMS II, (The Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT), and Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC). Other nonfunctional training includes BSNCOC, and Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88K on ACT for more information.', '732be4bb5fbcbe31d9d7f578e4a5fc8b40f4c836b21c9f823576085e9da9dd55', 18, 18, '18', 91, null, null, false, null),
  ('b91696a9-d804-57f9-8236-a088bcafbe20', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'In addition to the Broadening Assignments listed above, the Army Enlisted Aide Program is an opportunity open to all NCOs to serve on the personal staff of a general/flag officer. It is not recommended for a NCO to serve back-to-back tours in special assignments.', '622f797c8f5aea6968a06a4c00fea511a14c4444e5bcac220599e31b6e97b46b', 18, 18, '18', 92, null, null, false, null),
  ('290cecf9-6b46-578a-afae-7d4b1038ff9b', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'In preparation for promotion to MSG, complete all phases of SLC. Attend Master Leader Course (MLC), if selected. Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education Course I (SEJPME I).', '541ba08e5b644e03a031015989372cd207c14a54afbaf0de5b67f577061785cc', 18, 18, '18', 93, null, null, false, null),
  ('a9fe4966-d2d1-5bb3-81dd-c5541fa5edcc', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'SFCs should maintain a good balance of generating and operating force assignments that enhance a Soldier’s experience, knowledge, and career progression. NCOs who have served successfully and frequently in challenging leadership positions are considered more competitive for promotion than those who have not.', 'e11695240e9b66e6e14f188d5c7992a4a97a43678391fef50669c0796cc839b8', 18, 18, '18', 94, null, null, false, null),
  ('f591e213-eea8-5b8a-8297-5f218e77d0a4', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'The 88K SFC must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Platoon Sergeant, Detachment Sergeant, Small Tug Vessel Master, First Mate, Marine Operations NCO, Operations Sergeant, or Boatswain.', '1f1fc81d65547a1942ebfda7da669a5f16ed7871e869e33f8c76a2c4ab383d92', 18, 18, '18', 95, null, null, false, null),
  ('46f56a8e-b079-572e-ae62-00e52160a9a8', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, SLC Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Training Developer, and Watercraft Operator (SATMO).', '92ea95ea4cf2278ab279cb2b0d204548ffd76fa835f3bef6bd97c061384d3a1f', 18, 18, '18', 96, null, null, false, null),
  ('91012f3b-ae5c-51ab-bb66-38a777eebe5f', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SFCs for the next higher grade.
1. Most qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions: Detachment Sergeant, Platoon Sergeant, Small Tug Vessel Master, First Mate, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course.
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault; Airborne; Ranger School.
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Marine Operations NCO; Operations Sergeant.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant; SLC Instructor; AIT Instructor; Marine Operations NCO (SATMO); Training Developer.
2. Highly qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in a position such as Detachment Sergeant, Platoon Sergeant, Small Tug Vessel Master, First Mate.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Marine Standardization Examiner (MSE); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Operations Sergeant; Marine Operations NCO.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Drill Sergeant, SLC Instructor, AIT Instructor, Marine Operations NCO (SATMO), Training Developer.', '2c896e9ff44d4d5463d7e1d87e978318311af0b414faecac8bdd585bc0cf6bad', 18, 19, '18', 97, null, null, false, null),
  ('7e5c0a97-a72b-57e3-bd83-a9fe7a31e311', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'skills', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Leadership, Management, Multi-Domain Collaboration, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Reasoning, General Communication, Safety & Compliance, Training and Developing Others, and Tactical/Technical Competence.', '2bc5ee207ccb7ce1dddf4a5a4362f7809cc9829481c005e6a61d18152b3e650d', 19, 19, '19', 98, null, null, false, null),
  ('c9d2389f-42a9-556c-a686-9c84136ed4da', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Complete associate degree. The completion of an associate degree conveys initiative and potential. Begin pursuing a bachelor’s degree or other higher-level education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', 'be21889698c9bbb1d53f5bed3774e7dbc99499dcbaa8b018ee35de61ddcef137', 19, 19, '19', 99, null, null, false, null),
  ('b1c0d356-e8c0-5517-82dd-99335eaaa05c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'Functional training includes continued work on certification, BMR, Global Maritime Distress and Safety System, and MROC. Aside from skill level certification to grade, other training includes TC-AIMS II, (The Transportation Coordinators’-Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC), and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional; however important training includes BSNCOC, and Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88K on ACT for more information.', '78016d279b93b18fd7554be677844d2239fd86771c95cf22d24250f9f6183456', 19, 19, '19', 100, null, null, false, null),
  ('2bb29303-faa7-5dfe-af1d-74e1073f39a0', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88K', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military occupational specialty 88K Watercraft Operator', 'In addition to the Broadening Assignments listed above, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), SARC, Assistant Inspector General, and Army Enlisted Aide are opportunities a 88K SFC can pursue. It is not recommended for a NCO to serve in back-to- back tours in special assignments.Army career degrees. See SOCAD Army Degree Program.
(4) Master Sergeant/First Sergeant and Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major. See Chapter 25.', 'ee977d0fb09203e16fe6b9e5b6b2b0f5d2c63e892bbd733099cb37ef12f55b49', 20, 20, '20', 101, null, null, false, null),
  ('b07f9223-2083-50a7-89df-e1f686b2b033', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Watercraft Engineer Course. Attend Basic Leader Course (BLC), if possible. Obtaining recognition as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Distinguished Leader, Honor Graduate, or Commandant’s List in BLC should be a goal. Attend Watercraft Engineer Certification Course (Course# 652-F2), no earlier than 24 months after completing 88L AIT but prior to promotion to SGT, to attain MOS certifications required IAW AR 56-9 to serve in 20 level positions on vessels.', 'cd171c8298691ab453f974354dc9b8c066ae4105a8eb276949a0e8d152c699a7', 20, 20, '20', 102, null, null, false, null),
  ('460cc9fb-f8fa-59a1-950f-aaae5c1a237c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'These include positions focused on the functional aspect of the MOS at the company level, which build a strong base of technical expertise in equipment, MOS skills, and common Soldier tasks. Positions such as Marine Engineman allow the Soldier to gainfunctional and leadership experience.', '6f6206ec7af22c9a32e2440a992fb23f4275b277f2ff53e361b41a7c396f8573', 21, 21, '21', 103, null, null, false, null),
  ('0058b7af-9c74-5599-b1e2-f9e1749de45a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', '(c) Promotion indicators. Indicators a Soldier has promotion potential include maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards, consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities, and consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
(d) Attributes must reflect: One that is culturally astute, agility, adaptability, and resiliency.', '156c4246002ca95fd596bea966786ef1c903ecd4d4926b0babe886562cf7981c', 21, 21, '21', 104, null, null, false, null),
  ('1be4b431-7e2f-5f94-9bbc-84617b115312', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Begin pursuing an associate degree or higher-level civilian education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '22ce38707bac4005d5823c458ff5b7cab6c465432437ddc1116c35164ab540a0', 21, 21, '21', 105, null, null, false, null),
  ('b99b78de-1d61-59c4-95d1-dad579e599f2', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'L10 Certification and L20 Certification. Training and certification to grade remain top priority at this level. Aside from skill level certification to grade, other training includes TC-AIMS II, (The Transportation Coordinators-Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88L on ACT for more information.', '36088fc8f79d05b77ee9ebf32361921495b9117652a44cba13d33befb2703df9', 21, 21, '21', 106, null, null, false, null),
  ('c9c0be0a-bb4f-5e4c-9d51-dd41303e10cc', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'N/A', 'e2f79e5b60330bba4c289962231b6ba2957d0b14e7deb3110417003c79dea635', 21, 21, '21', 107, null, null, false, null),
  ('b613ad2d-5b2e-5f13-9fac-7baaca65adbf', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'In preparation for promotion to SSG, complete BLC. Attend Watercraft Engineer Advanced Leader Course (ALC), prior to promotion to SSG to attain 30 level MOS certifications required IAW 56-9 to serve in 30 level positions on vessels. Graduating with honors from ALC should be a goal.', '748d2655657df583cd11fb34483b43c841689f59b538c5bab98ea07717e1f292', 21, 21, '21', 108, null, null, false, null),
  ('1c75f689-df6a-59f8-a25b-3066de6c109a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Focus on assignments at the company level that develop leadership skills and enhance technical and tactical skills. Seek assignments that provide an opportunity to serve in a leadership position. NCO that seek tough demanding positions are considered more competitive than those who do not.', '3f1c7ac9f459b812023490a448f47b6c5dbd6439ba077c606d7e14b7603be5a4', 21, 21, '21', 109, null, null, false, null),
  ('194445d3-2926-5ec1-aa51-f9fd2f275a77', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'The 88L SGT must seek out key leadership positions as a Senior Marine Engineman or Marine Maintenance NCO.', '109e9936ac27f23c6cd29b6369506c78c4a9dd3182aae7d6247dc67e98304c27', 21, 21, '21', 110, null, null, false, null),
  ('f785b767-1009-55a7-8793-68f743814c19', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', '(d) Promotion indicators.
1. Strong NCOERs that reflect superior performance and potential in a variety of challenging assignments.
2. Exceeded course standards (Honor Graduate and Commandant’s List).
3. Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
4. Consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities.
5. Consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
(e)Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned as a Senior Marine Engineman.Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Tactical/Technical Competence, Teamwork, Systems Thinking, Mechanical & Electrical, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Reasoning, General Communication, and Safety & Compliance.', 'c50b49ac727ee287f00b51101f3f783f08dd44c8cb2854294786074236660361', 21, 22, '21', 111, null, null, false, null),
  ('40ad31bc-4521-512a-bd37-73e8bd985d35', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Continue pursuit of associate degree or higher-level civilian education. NCO of the Month/Quarter/Year Boards. For additional information on self-development, refer Chapter 3.', 'e0cd11a6d4172669d7332327349712c611a2f04de61fe0ad48d0a6bd6e88484e', 22, 22, '22', 112, null, null, false, null),
  ('eccbdba9-e7d1-5e39-af03-420ac2c73ed4', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Continue with watercraft skill level certifications. Other training includes TC-AIMS II (Transportation Coordinators’ Automated Information for Movements System II), Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88L on ACT for more information.', 'f4fead48327cc16f3068c9a5265b86326f50caa6efe990b4b8802cc979af99fb', 22, 22, '22', 113, null, null, false, null),
  ('d521fe22-8855-5886-b21c-359826b1c514', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Drill Sergeant; Recruiter.', '851f2b6221d0dedcd105001f6dc5da2405c93043234f8d0fe14f2a807b4d88c7', 22, 22, '22', 114, null, null, false, null),
  ('061c4c14-ce14-5652-96e3-5a09572f624d', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Attend Watercraft Engineer Senior Leader Course (SLC) to attain 40 level certifications required IAW AR 56-9 to serve in 40 level positions on vessels. Attend Transportation Deployment/Distribution Senior Leader Course (SLC), if possible. Graduating with honors from SLC should be a goal.', '22f86816589810808e188634595ff25431507b3e404dfd043055cc47b8400d5a', 22, 22, '22', 115, null, null, false, null),
  ('be9b89f5-59db-5bef-bfa0-2a91a738a4e2', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Seek assignments at company and BN levels focused on continued development and refinement of leadership skills and tactical and technical expertise. Seek out the tough leadership positions and excel in the performance of the duties associated with those positions. These positions offer unique opportunities in the areas of leadership and problem solving.
(f) Career Development assignments. The 88L SSG must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Assistant Marine Engineer, Junior Marine Engineer, Marine Maintenance SGT, and Watercraft Engineer. Recommend SSGs obtain 24 months experience in a critical leader development position.', '12c9773400a744e736315b86c2118992cb357d0e901a85b84e8932b0257c4754', 22, 22, '22', 116, null, null, false, null),
  ('98688266-71e5-52c0-a213-8affeeb10572', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Key opportunities include ALC Instructor, Recruiter, and Junior Marine Engineer (SATMO).', '6839b1c48e5352b4baa0ada5cede12798c53da4601b2ca624493e3fba7cc3848', 22, 22, '22', 117, null, null, false, null),
  ('b580d4bd-01d3-5449-945e-4913673e5147', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SSGs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions Assistant Mariner Engineer, Junior Marine Engineer, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC- AIMS II (Functional User); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES).
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault Course; Airborne Course; Ranger School.
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Marine Maintenance Sergeant; Watercraft Engineer.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Recruiter; ALC Instructor; Junior Marine Engineer (SATMO).
2. Highly qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in positions, such as, Assistant Marine Engineer; Junior Marine Engineer.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued civilian education and earned credit hours towards a degree.
(e) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Marine Standardization Examiner (MSE).
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Marine Maintenance Sergeant, Watercraft Engineer.
(g) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Recruiter, ALC Instructor, Junior Marine Engineer (SATMO).
(f) Attributes must reflect. Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Management, Training and Developing Others, General Communication, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Teamwork, Mechanical & Electrical, and Safety & Compliance.', 'd1a211ac9f79ff0ed1c579e1b7eee0d5f0c91193753e917b8f8087dce3bedfb5', 22, 23, '22', 118, null, null, false, null),
  ('de6eef0f-00b7-58ad-af08-b7ac752f7df0', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to paragraph 26–3. Continue AA/AS. Continue pursuing higher-level civilian education opportunities, with a goal of completing an associate degree. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '5eeb66f09478c8d364137799776cb6e53cb059d629bad1f0732d4164957aaf3e', 23, 23, '23', 119, null, null, false, null),
  ('718f85ce-5e58-5c23-b9f9-91472bc61017', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Continue with watercraft skill level certifications. Other training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’ Automated Information for Movements System II), Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Senior Transportation Operations Course, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Additional nonfunctional training includes BSNCOC, and Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88L on ACT for more information.', '7afb5510eaa01c7b7d4638b10ccaacc259ed2f154d18fac167eef273cccf9929', 23, 23, '23', 120, null, null, false, null),
  ('6ca4ac7e-4bc8-54cf-9447-6ee09b870892', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'In addition to the Broadening Assignments listed above, the Army Enlisted Aide Program is an opportunity open to all NCOs to serve on the personal staff of a general/flag officer. It is not recommended for an NCO to serve back-to-back tours in a special assignment.', '4fb4c8932d703d886397272a5740f6fd687d719ee52f6b6d6128301784071950', 23, 23, '23', 121, null, null, false, null),
  ('aae44da3-7f1c-5610-9758-872dd41ab6bb', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'In preparation for promotion to MSG, complete SLC. Attend Master Leader Course (MLC), if selected. Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education Course I (SEJPME I).', 'e7c418cd6c2daa6f9f0b6f1db2b499e7f1d5e7e664805d7d5e250afd81c32195', 24, 24, '24', 122, null, null, false, null),
  ('6d079219-b285-59cb-a0e5-8a57f2525c24', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'SFCs should maintain a good balance of generating and operating force assignments that enhance a Soldier’s experience, knowledge, and career progression. NCOs who have served successfully and frequently in challenging leadership positions are considered more competitive for promotion than those who have not.', 'e11695240e9b66e6e14f188d5c7992a4a97a43678391fef50669c0796cc839b8', 24, 24, '24', 123, null, null, false, null),
  ('ec39c861-043b-5f4a-b814-bb32e4450b26', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'The 88L SFC must seek out leadership and developmental positions as Platoon Sergeant, Assistant Engineer, Small Tug Chief Engineer, Marine Maintenance Supervisor, and Marine Maintenance NCO.', '88686723b364c032ed50ae4ea3f6992963d4da258f5b24c135274ec3ea74e671', 24, 24, '24', 124, null, null, false, null),
  ('0b549fb9-06af-58b4-bf66-5e4232f14f23', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, SLC Instructor, Training Developer, and Marine Maintenance NCO (SATMO).', '7a2e0766d7234e13f456f0dcf89784f7b1098a2d4c46cf7234626a1a9b1537ba', 24, 24, '24', 125, null, null, false, null),
  ('ae1c84d8-35f2-591e-80c9-eee80cd99f7e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SFCs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions Platoon Sergeant, Assistant Engineer, Small Tug Chief Engineer, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC- AIMS II (Functional User); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES).
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault; Airborne; Ranger School.
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Marine Maintenance Supervisor, or Marine Maintenance NCO.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as SLC Instructor, AIT Instructor, Marine Maintenance NCO (SATMO), Training Developer.
2. Highly qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in one of the following positions Platoon Sergeant, Assistant Engineer, or Small Tug Chief Engineer.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Marine Standardization Examiner (MSE).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Marine Maintenance NCO, or Marine Maintenance Supervisor.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as SLC Instructor, AIT Instructor, Marine Maintenance NCO (SATMO), Training Developer.
(f) Attributes must reflect—Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Management, Multi-Domain Collaboration, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Systems Thinking, General Communication, Mechanical & Electrical, and Safety & Compliance.', '3e3f86233af5a2f675621b605ee5bf1e94070e55677cf81583b8d6c49cbdcb3a', 24, 25, '24', 126, null, null, false, null),
  ('1a1ecb02-ba94-57a1-aad1-3cc0432c4f05', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Complete associate degree. The completion of an associate degree conveys initiative and potential. Begin pursuing a bachelor’s degree or other higher-level education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, See Chapter 3.', 'd42cf9a9641f15daeb4a144b152ded89d2a418680eb75181975ab8f0fd319e96', 25, 25, '25', 127, null, null, false, null),
  ('a902ae2c-6ba9-5bab-a49d-2b07b82a9776', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'Continue watercraft skill level certifications. Aside from skill level certification to grade, other training includes TC-AIMS II, (The Transportation Coordinators’ Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC), and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional; however important training includes BSNCOC, and Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications, a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88L on ACT for more information.', '804db0d2e15fd82f264719202ed0504a5b0b39c9d3baeccb5b1a8afb0703a68b', 25, 25, '25', 128, null, null, false, null),
  ('c9220052-c56d-589c-992e-b1a61ee5ae2a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'In addition to the Broadening Assignments listed above, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), SARC, Recruiter, and Army Enlisted Aide are opportunities 88L SFCs can pursue. It is not recommended for a NCO to serve back-to-back tours in special assignments.', 'aa6eac295e51f855930d12f766ac79d299e61e5cb57c411f9b18a67438ccab39', 25, 25, '25', 129, null, null, false, null),
  ('1a210a76-0145-54aa-aa37-75a721877d85', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88L', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army career degrees', 'Chapter 10. Military occupational specialty 88L Watercraft Engineer', 'See SOCAD Army Degree Program.
(5) Master Sergeant/First Sergeant and Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major. See Chapter 25.', 'f946bd2819a57b16cd9c6df082bd8f42e0627f6191dab7a9b4445b87d6f5206b', 25, 25, '25', 130, null, null, false, null),
  ('38e45741-8ab4-5aa5-a79b-80bddc9d63a6', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — overview', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', '(e) Institutional Training. Motor Transport Operator Course. Attend Basic Leader Course (BLC), if possible. Obtaining recognition as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Distinguished Leader, Honor Graduate or Commandant’s List in BLC should be a goal.
(f) Operational assignments. These include positions at the company level focused on building a strong base of technical expertise in basic MOS skills and common Soldier tasks. Soldiers should seek assignments such as Vehicle Driver, Heavy Vehicle Driver, HET Vehicle Driver, Dispatcher, and Driver.
(g) Promotion indicators. Indicators a Soldier has promotion potential include maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards, consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities, and consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
(h) Attributes must reflect: One that is culturally astute, agility, adaptability, and resiliency
(i) Self-development. Begin pursuing an associate degree or higher-level civilian education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.
(j) Additional training. This includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’-Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications, a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88M on ACT for more information.
(k) Special assignments. Special assignments for 88M Soldiers include, but are not limited to, positions within Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), United States Army Special Operations Command (USASOC), 1st Special Forces Command (SFC), United States Army JFK Special Warfare Center and School (USAJFKSWCS75th Ranger Regiment, , and Special Mission Units (SMU). Soldiers assigned to these commands could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. These positions are considered career-enhancing assignments and successful service makes someone considered to be best qualified for promotion.
(l) Army career degrees. See SOCAD Army Degree Program.', 'd33c8c37b2e2425aa9b075d3339535f5763efc6a6ede131345567cbe47d161a5', 26, 27, '26', 131, null, null, false, null),
  ('032470bd-d9e6-597e-a67e-248bc01e117a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — overview', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', '(e) Institutional Training. In preparation for promotion to SSG, complete BLC. Attend Motor Transport Operator Advanced Leader Course (ALC), if possible. Graduating with honors from ALC should be a goal.
(f) Operational assignments. Focus on assignments at the company level that develop your leadership skills and enhance your technical and tactical skills. Seek assignments that provide an opportunity to serve in a leadership position. NCOs who have served frequently in tough jobs and are successful are considered more competitive than those who have not.
(g) Career Development assignments. The 88M SGT must seek out key leadership positions as a Senior Vehicle Driver, Dispatcher, Operations Sergeant, Assistant Operations Sergent, Training Management NCO, Heavy Vehicle Driver, Chauffer, Courier, Drivers Test Sergeant, and Training NCO.
(h) Promotion indicators.
1. Strong NCOERs that reflect superior performance and potential in a variety of challenging assignments.
2. Exceeded course standards (Honor Graduate and Commandant’s List).
3. Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
4. Consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities.
5. Consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
6. Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned as a Dispatcher, Senior Vehicle Driver, Heavy Vehicle Driver, Driver, Chauffer, and Operations Sergeant.
(i) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Tactical/Technical Competence, Teamwork, Decision Making, Situational Awareness, Psychomotor Ability, Problem Solving, Management, Training and Developing Others, and Safety & Compliance.
(j) Self-development. Continue pursuit of associate degree or higher-level civilian education. NCO of the Month/Quarter/Year Boards. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.
(k) Additional training. This training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC), Global Air Transportation Execution Systems-Surface (GATES), and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88M on ACT for more information.
(l) Special assignments. Special assignments for 88M SGTs include, but are not limited to, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, White House Communications Agency (WHCA), Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), United States Army Special Operations Command (USASOC), 1st Special Forces Command (SFC), United States Army JFK Special Warfare Center and School (USAJFKSWCS), 75th Ranger Regiment, and Special Mission Units (SMU). NCOs assigned to these commands could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. These positions are considered as career enhancing assignments and successful service makes someone considered to be best qualified for promotion.
(i) Army career degrees. See SOCAD Army Degree Program.', 'bee7374a28f0a3b6dd8c6e796a4bafac882259053654575b0a9ebb845e559b1c', 27, 28, '27', 132, null, null, false, null),
  ('c4a0570c-acce-598f-acd1-2d9e5ea3178a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — overview', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', '(e) Institutional Training. In preparation for promotion to SFC, complete ALC. Attend Transportation Deployment/Distribution Senior Leader Course (SLC), if possible. Graduating with honors from SLC should be a goal.
(f) Operational assignments. Seek assignments in the Operating Force at the company and BN levels focused on continued development and refinement of leadership skills and tactical and technical expertise. Seek out the tough leadership positions and excel in the performance of the duties associated with those positions. These positions offer unique opportunities in the areas of leadership and problem solving.
(g) Career Development assignments. The 88M SSG must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Squad Leader, Section Sergeant, Senior Vehicle Operator, Master Driver Trainer, Operations Sergeant, Senior Driver, Heavy Vehicle Driver, and Chauffer. Recommend SSGs obtain 24 months experience in a critical leader development position.
(h) Broadening assignments. Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Training Developer, ALC Instructor, BLC Small Group Leader, Recruiter, Observer Controller/Trainer, Courier and positions with the White House Transportation Agency or White House Communications Agency. Superior performance in these types of positions sets NCOs apart from their peers.
(i) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SSGs for the next higher grade.
1. Most qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:', '1cfa3c0875b0585875ef17e17289b5c8e9a4d01bd8044f794cde2665767c7271', 28, 28, '28', 133, null, null, false, null),
