  ('edf724b1-e005-5f73-994b-e5f3526e4045', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', 'Special assignments for 88M SSGs include, but are not limited to, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, White House Transportation Agency (WHTA), Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), United States Army Special Operations Command (USASOC), 1st Special Forces Command (SFC), United States Army JFK Special Warfare Center and School (USAJFKSWCS), 75th Ranger Regiment, 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment (SOAR), and Special Mission Units (SMU). Soldiers assigned to these commands could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. These positions are considered as career enhancing assignments and successful service makes someone considered to be best qualified for promotion.', '755a5964d6ce732b7bc210eac450c05f607b47a632b1f315a78b4e30f4f26157', 29, 30, '29', 141, null, null, false, null),
  ('840c13af-6629-56a2-9a7e-62ae2f024544', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', 'In preparation for promotion to MSG, complete SLC. Attend Master Leader Course (MLC), if selected. Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education Course I (SEJPME I).', 'e7c418cd6c2daa6f9f0b6f1db2b499e7f1d5e7e664805d7d5e250afd81c32195', 30, 30, '30', 142, null, null, false, null),
  ('0228ffc0-ca6e-5a39-9d88-412ee9bb8b0a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', 'SFCs should maintain a good balance of generating and operating force assignments that enhance a Soldier’s experience, knowledge, and career progression. NCOs who have served successfully and frequently in tough leadership positions are considered more competitive for promotion than those who have not.', '804e82f85c689545eb3d4a1cd1abbc5cd04bd3b2a189ae35a5e43ba8adf9fac1', 30, 30, '30', 143, null, null, false, null),
  ('84c66d65-77d7-5ea7-bea5-a1984b05d987', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', 'The 88M SFC must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Platoon Sergeant, Detachment Sergeant, Section Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, Truckmaster, Highway Operations Sergeant, Master Driver, Master Driver Trainer, Chauffer. The Platoon Sergeant positions is key for successful development within the Sustainment Warfighting Function. Recommended time in this critical position is 24- 36 months.', 'cbc00303ce5744d948f62e60ee4da8d1be09cbda337f6de631069d9acb71c335', 30, 30, '30', 144, null, null, false, null),
  ('0604105e-9c48-5f4f-95ed-e6e318ff2116', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', 'Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, Recruiter, Logistics Advisor NCOIC (SFAB), Presidential Support Driver (WHTA), Highway Operations Sergeant (WHTA), BLC Senior Small Group Leader, ALC/SLC Instructor, Talent Management NCO (HRC), Training Developer, Inspector General NCO, Observer Controller/Trainer, Sexual Assault Response Coordinator, Equal Opportunity Advisor, Tactical NCO, and Training with Industry.', 'd4d124df1d0a5a1a4112200c41141457a8e0f6f3212072f74fd3c0a4b721c186', 30, 30, '30', 145, null, null, false, null),
  ('514f4a88-9828-5b69-9279-41f6f818d53f', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88M', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 13. Military occupational specialty 88M Motor Transport Operator', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SFCs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions: Platoon Sergeant, Section Sergeant, Truckmaster, Detachment Sergeant or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff (ASI 2S); Master Finess Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Course; Support Operations Course; Senior Transportation Operations Course; Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Air Assault; Airborne; SHARP; Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); Integrated Computerized Deployment Systems (ICODES).
(e) Attended other training, such as, Ranger School, Air Assault, Airborne.
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Highway Operations Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, Master Driver, Master Driver Trainer, Chauffer. Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Logistics Advisor NCOIC (SFAB), AIT Instructor, BLC SSGL, ALC Instructor, SLC Instructor, Recruiter, Observer Controller/Trainer, Presidential Support Driver or Highway Operations Sergeant (White House Transportation Agency), Inspector General NCO, Training With Industry, Equal Opportunity Advisor, Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC), Talent Management NCO (HRC), Training Developer, Tactical NCO (U.S. Military Academy West Point).
2. Highly qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in positions such as Platoon Sergeant, Truckmaster, Section Sergeant.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Commercial Drivers License (CDL); Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; License Instructor/License Examiner (LI/LE).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Highway Operations Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, Master Driver, Master Driver Trainer, Chauffer.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Logistics Advisor NCOIC (SFAB), AIT Instructor, BLC SSGL, ALC Instructor, SLC Instructor, Recruiter, Observer Controller/Trainer, Presidential Support Driver or Highway Operations Sergeant (White House Transportation Agency), Inspector General NCO, Training With Industry, Equal Opportunity Advisor, Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC), Talent Management NCO (HRC), Training Developer, Tactical NCO (U.S. Military Academy Weste Point).
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Decision Making, Management, Problem Solving, Multi-Domain Collaboration, Situational Awareness, Reasoning, Safety & Compliance, Training and Developing Others, and General Communication.', '16943e1df664e0bf7fb75e3541a0fb385a18e8cd13c8af196503a30c0e059b79', 30, 31, '30', 146, null, null, false, null),
