(d) Attributes must reflect: One that is culturally astute, agility, adaptability, and resiliency.', '156c4246002ca95fd596bea966786ef1c903ecd4d4926b0babe886562cf7981c', 33, 33, '33', 154, null, null, false, null),
  ('6dc126af-9e45-5003-ae3a-3e91c6e3be5f', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Begin pursuing an associate degree or higher-level civilian education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '22ce38707bac4005d5823c458ff5b7cab6c465432437ddc1116c35164ab540a0', 33, 33, '33', 155, null, null, false, null),
  ('518dbdaa-4d5a-5552-8068-37cc1bc59317', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Functional training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II), Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP), Global Air Trans Execution System (GATES), Unit Movement Officer-Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC), and Joint Container Management Course. Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88N on ACT for more information.', '518de780850d22345be83d6ddefeaa4ad788fdfbfd09aae80b90d45dc8887546', 33, 33, '33', 156, null, null, false, null),
  ('b2daa89c-edca-5355-a52d-4afc0dc323b4', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Special assignments for 88N Soldiers include, but are not limited to, positions in 1st Special Forces Command (SFC), and United States Army JFK Special Warfare Center and School (USAJFKSWCS). These positions are considered as career enhancing assignments and successful service makes someone considered to be best qualified for promotion.', '3055c31c8ee080d09529b427ec497de262e0d0be0a1a4368222b45d79a9cf87a', 33, 33, '33', 157, null, null, false, null),
  ('6bdb6a3d-6a79-58f8-934f-bc8b4413fc04', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'In preparation for promotion to SSG, complete BLC. Attend Transportation Management Coordinator Advanced Leader Course (ALC), is possible. Graduating with honors from ALC should be a goal.', '389707f10394f493a01c1c8b103d0133efa8fa9c6c3b3a49ca42a09634b872c1', 33, 33, '33', 158, null, null, false, null),
  ('a56910fd-53c5-5da0-ac19-14dad1e22fad', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Focus on assignments that develop leadership skills and enhance technical and tactical skills. 88N NCOs, based on authorized positions, are not always afforded the opportunity to serve in leadership positions. However, there are assignments that involve leadership responsibility and 88N SGTs should take advantage of any opportunity to serve in a leadership role.', 'd1bd6b863b5a88c7804dc6c9a13e9203852f9747384f542daa80269d2ca6da34', 33, 33, '33', 159, null, null, false, null),
  ('cd1a43cd-2a2e-5a61-bdfa-ac862e87e233', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'The 88N SGT must seek out positions as Movements NCO, or Transportation Management NCO. To gain leadership experience 88N SGTs should seek out opportunities within these positions to serve in a leadership role.', 'fd4af7e124a73faea04addbea43816bebc2b94a1d5a892b47cebb3672fd7a3f2', 33, 33, '33', 160, null, null, false, null),
  ('3c1f0617-b1a9-5019-acea-740b04ef0c6c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', '(d) Promotion indicators.
1. Strong NCOERs that reflect superior performance and potential in a variety of challenging assignments.
2. Exceeded course standards (Honor Graduate and Commandant’s List).
3. Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
4. Consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities.
5. Consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
6. Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned as a Transportation Management NCO or Movements NCO.
(e) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Decision Making, Situational Awareness, General Cognitive Ability, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Stress Tolerance, Active Listening, Teamwork, and Training & Developing Others.', 'e15a0ed4a8a5c51e9bbc565072122d70afbda40dfd3525ef01842f645ac090c2', 33, 34, '33', 161, null, null, false, null),
  ('e1a5bae1-6c70-52c0-a6f7-ed36db458f89', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Continue pursuit of associate degree or higher-level civilian education. NCO of the Month/Quarter/Year Boards. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', 'c66bbdffd7a3e7d9c9d196863573a318e51a233cd1c6f42e5fdfbf8702d2f3e1', 34, 34, '34', 162, null, null, false, null),
  ('e12507a0-a3bb-5406-a142-109bfe484bda', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Functional training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II), Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning (ADP), and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP), Global Air Trans Execution System (GATES), Unit Movement Officer-Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC), and Joint Container Management Course, and Joint Operations Planning and Execution System (JOPES). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88N on ACT for more information.', '6cdda784c2d789b05ef44a4956182d51945181546a9dbc9dcb1410bf7a0b8af8', 34, 34, '34', 163, null, null, false, null),
  ('d730ce25-37ca-5ad2-a442-6bc867424510', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Special assignments for 88N SGTs include, but are not limited to, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, White House Communications Agency (WHCA), United States Army Special Operations Command (USASOC), 1st Special Forces Command (SFC), 75th Ranger Regiment, and Special Mission Units (SMU). Soldiers assigned to these commands could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. These positions are considered as career enhancing assignments and successful service makes someone considered to be best qualified for promotion.', 'bff06fbd600bb37e45a9ce8ea1aa3392847a6d329eefbe47a64b0015855ab89c', 34, 34, '34', 164, null, null, false, null),
  ('833bfd75-bef4-5659-b7e6-4d41ababac32', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'In preparation for promotion to SFC, complete ALC. Attend Transportation Deployment/Distribution Senior Leader Course (SLC), if possible. Graduating with honors from SLC should be a goal.', '0a466b6b0457a2e6eafcd410bcff13fd44cad573b7c2fa2c51e24286f300527a', 34, 34, '34', 165, null, null, false, null),
  ('3fab442b-10ee-5477-9ce6-446f6185dbb5', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Seek assignments focused on continued development and refinement of leadership skills and tactical and technical expertise; seek to become a functional expert in your MOS. 88N NCOs, based on authorized positions, are not always afforded the opportunity to serve in leadership positions. However, there are assignments that involve leadership responsibility and 88N SSGs should take advantage of any opportunity to serve in a leadership role. Positions such as a Movements Supervisor, Movements NCO, or Transportation Management Supervisor are viewed as equivalent to holding a position as a section or squad leader. Seek out the tough leadership positions and excel in the performance of the duties associated with those positions. These positions offer unique opportunities in the areas of leadership and problem solving.', 'bbc5fc97f1e31ed6dde229f6cc8389338bcda9ed96f6a9df1f34ce51e3e16762', 34, 35, '34', 166, null, null, false, null),
  ('df2f8e8d-bcb5-5cbc-ae41-5a486fc5bdac', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'The 88N SSG must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as Movements Supervisor, Transportation Management Supervisor, Movements NCO. Recommend SSGs obtain 24 months experience in a critical leader development position.', '2b6b854c0c58adc0583eb748963659999eb9187be5f87a8be981dcfdbe5f475a', 35, 35, '35', 167, null, null, false, null),
  ('1aa7a99c-f3c1-556d-92f2-a3ab2cabf93d', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, ALC Instructor, Joint Mobility Operations NCO, Joint Air Transportation NCO, JOPES Planning NCO, Force Generation NCO, Observer Controller/Trainer. Superior performance in these types of positions sets NCOs apart from their peers.', '5b52e103677bfcf09fed23fe81099c585a3e05310c24f97345f11c812dc50a9c', 35, 35, '35', 168, null, null, false, null),
  ('32d6f50c-a6bd-51c4-a315-38766f963ec0', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SSGs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions Transportation Management Supervisor, Movements Supervisor, of positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff (ASI 2S); Master Fitness Training (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Course; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Support Operations Course; Senior Transportation Operations Course.
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault, Airborne, Ranger School
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Movements NCO.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor; ALC Instructor; Drill Sergeant; Recruiter; Joint Mobility Operations NCO; Joint Air Transportation NCO; JOPES Planning NCO; Force Generation NCO; Observer Controller/Trainer (OC/T).
2. Highly qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in positions such as Movements Supervisor, Transportation Management Supervisor (equivalent to a section or squad leader).
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Unit Movement Officer Deployment Plannint Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Joint Operational Planning and Execution Systems (JOPES).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Movements NCO.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor, ALC Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Joint Mobility Operations NCO, Joint Air Transportation NCO, JOPES Planning NCO, Force Generation NCO, Observer Controller/Trainer (OC/T).
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Management, Decision Making, Situational Awareness, General Cognitive Ability, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Stress Tolerance, Active Listening, Safety & Compliance and Training & Developing Others.', '7ff0632f1af1bc727b26d05a42895c5d4530de4e52b97975a97f819258e97360', 35, 36, '35', 169, null, null, false, null),
  ('d251147c-acd8-53b7-a108-171645a94031', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Continue pursuing higher-level civilian education opportunities, with a goal of completing an associate degree. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '5ec759dcb05ee5524faaa48ce1b0a45df30386ec8bfc1d2dda7daae62e745ab2', 36, 36, '36', 170, null, null, false, null),
  ('7ec347be-93f1-5aaa-b085-69e49e7a46de', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Functional training includes Integrated Data Environment (IDE) and/or Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, ADP, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP), Global Air Trans Execution System (GATES), TC-AIMS II, UMODPC, Joint Container Management Course, JOPES, and Senior Transportation Operations Course. Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional training includes BSNCOC, and the Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88N on ACT for more information.', '6f4eb5ab30ddc8e41fa68cb770f6e1ba162ff813839ace6bbef53e9910fd1307', 36, 36, '36', 171, null, null, false, null),
  ('ba9325aa-ae65-5e83-9be8-0ec234c69331', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Special assignments for 88N SSGs include, but are not limited to, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, and positions within White House Communications Agency (WHCA), Theater Special Operations Command (TSOC), United States Army Special Operations Command (USASOC), 1st Special Forces Command (SFC), 75th Ranger Regiment, Defense Logistics Agency, US Army Transportation Command, and Special Mission Units (SMU). Soldiers assigned to these commands could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. These positions are considered as career enhancing assignments and successful service makes someone considered best qualified for promotion. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88N on ACT for more information.', '581cb75071d4fd1e660feb8795fd23ae38075abd364e967e0248f7fc3b5b132e', 36, 36, '36', 172, null, null, false, null),
  ('50d7877b-7b04-5d3c-a69f-b0020a709633', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'In preparation for promotion to MSG, complete SLC. Attend Master Leader Course (MLC), if selected. Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education Course I (SEJPME I).', 'e7c418cd6c2daa6f9f0b6f1db2b499e7f1d5e7e664805d7d5e250afd81c32195', 36, 36, '36', 173, null, null, false, null),
  ('76ed15de-4c97-5bb5-abdc-aee13560f96e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'SFCs should maintain a good balance of generating and operating force assignments to enhance the NCO’s experience, knowledge, and career progression. 88N NCOs, based on authorized positions, are not always afforded the opportunity to serve in leadership positions. However, there are assignments that involve leadership responsibility and 88N SFCs should take advantage of any opportunity to serve in a leadership role.', '4802cae40f89c85ad9fa5c4b4b1febe3fa4e041d3b948ff6b34bed984832fa4c', 36, 36, '36', 174, null, null, false, null),
  ('19fd28d0-d7a9-56b9-ae43-7de637feb05a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'The 88N SFC must seek out key leadership and developmental positions as a Detachment Sergeant, Senior Movements NCO, Staff Movements NCO, Transportation Logistics NCO, and Chief Movements Supervisor. These positions have responsibilities equivalent to those of a Platoon Sergeant. Opportunities serving in a Platoon Sergeant capacity are key for successful development within the Sustainment Warfighting Function. Recommended time in these types of critical positions is 24-36 months.', '0e74e96223ebea4e1de6a646a5eb95039fbcccf9a01573b76f84ee18e34f284d', 36, 37, '36', 175, null, null, false, null),
  ('49e3f522-adad-5a4c-b100-5d10b7b7f7d7', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Key opportunities include AIT Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Logistics Advisor NCOIC (SFAB), Chief Movements Supervisor (WHTA), Observer Controller/Trainer (OC/T), Maintenance Logistician, Career Management NCO (TC Proponent), Talent Management NCO (HRC), SLC Instructor, Training Developer, SARC, Victim Advocate, Senior Training Management NCO; and UMODPC Instructor.', 'faa94b590ee10fdad862ae7bd1d5debbf8d4f29743681984d7666356bc6f6fa3', 37, 37, '37', 176, null, null, false, null),
  ('710b8164-9a75-5752-bcba-0051392e9e41', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', '(e) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SFCs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions Detachment Sergeant, Senior Movements NCO, Chief Movements Supervisor, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff (ASI 2S); Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Course; Master Driver Training (ASI M9); Support Operations Course; Senior Transportation Operations Course; Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course.
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault, Airborne, or Ranger School.
(f) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Staff Movements NCO, Operations Sergeant, Transportation Logistics NCO.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Logistics Advisor NCOIC (SFAB), Chief Movements Supervisor (WHTA), Observer Controller/Trainer (OC/T), Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC), Maintenance Logistician, Talent Management NCO (HRC), Career Management NCO (Transportation Corps Proponent), Training Developer, SLC Instructor, Victim Advocate (VA), Senior Training Management NCO, Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC) Instructor.
2. Highly qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in one of the following positions Detachment Sergeant, Senior Movements NCO, Chief Movements Supervisor.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Joint Operational Planning and Execution System (JOPES).
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Staff Movements NCO, Operations Sergeant, Transportation Logistics NCO.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Observer Controller/Trainer (OC/T), Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC), Maintenance Logistician, Talent Management NCO (HRC), Career Management NCO (Transportation Corps Proponent), Training Developer, SLC Instructor, Victim Advocate (VA), Senior Training Management NCO, Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC) Instructor.
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Management, Decision Making, Situational Awareness, Written Communication, Problem Solving, Reasoning, Stress Tolerance, Perceptual Speed & Accuracy, Systems Thinking, IT Programs & Systems and Conscientiousness.', 'f45e0aa2d77416508c101daa5bb496bb984f661b8943a527b4232a9cdbcc2fbb', 37, 38, '37', 177, null, null, false, null),
  ('c7f77c12-7d80-5f17-9b01-742a87507c70', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Complete associate degree. The completion of an associate degree conveys initiative and potential. Begin pursuing a bachelor’s degree or other higher-level education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', 'be21889698c9bbb1d53f5bed3774e7dbc99499dcbaa8b018ee35de61ddcef137', 38, 38, '38', 178, null, null, false, null),
  ('e257e9fa-23ca-569e-aa67-5584b34dd4b4', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Functional training includes Integrated Data Environment (IDE) and/or Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, ADP, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP), Global Air Trans Execution System (GATES), TC-AIMS II, UMODPC, Joint Container Management, JOPES, Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional training includes BSNCOC, and the Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88N on ACT for more information.', '270e5743684a6b37f8eea6589e0500f1058c4199d45e5c5d8ea9fa58c79ee450', 38, 38, '38', 179, null, null, false, null),
  ('e79b6b87-92e9-55f9-a857-ed37aca52de8', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'Special assignments for 88N SFCs include, but are not limited to, positions within White House Transportation Agency (WHTA), Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), Theater Special Operations Command (TSOC), United States Army Command (USASOC), 75th Ranger Regiment, and Special Mission Units (SMU). Soldiers assigned to these commands could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. These positions are considered as career enhancing assignments and successful service makes someone considered as best qualified for promotion.', '04ffedaa2b473f7ae7cad569cc49ab92483a8289d8b1d080d165d9c476bfd022', 38, 38, '38', 180, null, null, false, null),
  ('8e842df7-6581-5039-a76b-669745a4a32b', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88N', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army career degrees', 'Chapter 16. Military occupational specialty 88N Transportation Management', 'See SOCAD Army Degree Program.
(5) Master Sergeant/First Sergeant and Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major. See Chapter 25', '663e30b1f5b8f8c9a3afb65d4756f9651cfdcb29175995d1a658f2b7f479e86f', 38, 38, '38', 181, null, null, false, null),
  ('822c4166-eb04-508b-83a6-71f1efd9ef6b', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Railway Specialist Course. Attend Basic Leader Course (BLC), if possible. Obtaining recognition as Distinguished Honor Graduate, Distinguished Leader, Honor Graduate or Commandant’s List in BLC should be a goal.', 'b9ac532c4d343217187b97b80ecab965eb6a730d3887e494510168eb9272767c', 39, 39, '39', 182, null, null, false, null),
  ('734b36d1-2cde-50a4-9ff4-5018151a50e8', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'The focus during the early years should be geared toward building a strong base of technical expertise in basic MOS skills. Soldiers should seek responsibility and take advantage of opportunities to display their leadership skills and initiative during all collective training. May serve as Railway Specialist.', '82730223438afdcb70fad4f8ae0f899ed4ee102f3a2a726c0aee1fd71ac88674', 39, 39, '39', 183, null, null, false, null),
  ('4ef08b3f-13c5-540b-a20c-357bc7a6ec31', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', '(c) Promotion indicators.
1. Honor Graduate and Commandant’s List
2. Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
3. Consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities.
4. Consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
(d) Attributes must reflect: One that is culturally astute, agility, adaptability, and resiliency.', 'eb53ebb44f17ace24eda344a4f0bd8d0e76cf47882bbcff2c2c6a8eb31be1b59', 39, 39, '39', 184, null, null, false, null),
  ('4574cac6-b4a1-54a5-937c-91b13e29225d', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Begin pursuing an associate degree or higher-level civilian education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '22ce38707bac4005d5823c458ff5b7cab6c465432437ddc1116c35164ab540a0', 39, 39, '39', 185, null, null, false, null),
  ('c5a17178-291f-5984-bbf0-b46a27bff68e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Functional training includes Railroad track standards and maintenance training courses. Additional training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88U on ACT for more information.', '392a4248442d4081ae8450a03d7daabee8cd835cbf78c23f995bfb508b8254c5', 39, 39, '39', 186, null, null, false, null),
  ('57681123-d7a3-548c-9a5a-64a02db2b250', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 39, 39, '39', 187, null, null, false, null),
  ('72284ad8-940d-5371-b430-4732f7697907', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'In preparation to promotion to SSG, complete BLC. Attend Railway Specialist Advanced Leader Course (ALC), if possible. Graduating with honors from ALC should be a goal', '561fdd06817607cfc54147c630a2f9f0b3ea6c06dcc5298375aa6cb850583c34', 39, 39, '39', 188, null, null, false, null),
  ('e16a3afe-ff83-50d3-aed2-7975118e2b4a', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'The focus during this phase of development should be geared toward leadership refinement. Soldiers should seek greater levels of responsibility and positions, which challenge both their technical and tactical knowledge. May serve as a Railway Advisor.', '5df5bc222aa89923684b1ed2e10ccb05fba9e08c9a43107bbba394b10eac62d2', 40, 40, '40', 189, null, null, false, null),
  ('672176ee-83b7-5adc-a706-3cd79dc55e9c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', '(c) Promotion indicators.
1. Strong NCOERs that reflect superior performance and potential in a variety of challenging assignments.
2. Exceeded course standards (Honor Graduate and Commandant’s List).
3. Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
4. Consistently pursued education through military courses and civilian educational opportunities.
5. Consistently demonstrated high standards of conduct and adherence to Army values on and off duty.
6. Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned as a Railway Advisor.
7. Demonstrated career flexibility as shown by serving in a multimodal developmental position.
(d) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Tactical/Technical Competence, Teamwork, Decision Making, Situational Awareness, Psychomotor Ability, Problem Solving, Management, Training and Developing Others, and Safety & Compliance.', '3a26f81f7643b4e041e1aa48e4d22068c9af31a37a2e73ccf871552f52ac0767', 40, 40, '40', 190, null, null, false, null),
  ('a513f4d8-6e29-5fb9-a46e-37e1526a7f41', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Continue pursuit of associate degree or higher-level civilian education. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '25d98eb8ecd578882646cb5ee2c0ae58f8f762086e5c9310da32049ab522df44', 40, 40, '40', 191, null, null, false, null),
  ('38f53628-fc55-5d86-99d9-480738c63182', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Functional training includes railroad track standards and maintenance training courses. Additional training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE)/Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications, a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88U on ACT for more information.', '239b5a72f82975f0532571fa66d1c58cbfa59e26b62245f0eef54b45b04fe3ee', 40, 40, '40', 192, null, null, false, null),
  ('31e30e1f-c2f0-5548-8f83-9975b456df3f', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Drill Sergeant and Recruiter.', '1fb6c7e31198204950c2b050adca3c02f100feda7b53bcae3701a8af339ce8c0', 40, 40, '40', 193, null, null, false, null),
  ('c3759887-3ac2-5aa6-9ddf-acc07e6bf346', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'In preparation for promotion to SFC, complete ALC. Attend Transportation Deployment/Distribution Senior Leader Course (SLC) and Railway Specialist Senior Leader Course (SLC), if possible. Graduating with honors from SLC should be a goal.', '78986cf1a283754e457d7fd243051b25a57134f6b56871f7b26e56d78c945148', 40, 40, '40', 194, null, null, false, null),
  ('087afe46-6c9d-5b78-91c5-c9639d9ff0c7', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Focus must be on continued development and refinement of leadership skills and tactical and technical expertise; seek to become a functional expert in your MOS. Seek out the tough leadership positions and excel in the performance of the duties associated with those positions. These positions offer unique opportunities in the areas of leadership and problem solving.', '707e2e87bffc379967d280fc9ee0c747ebab2ba50d36ca0175510ee94c92a6cb', 40, 40, '40', 195, null, null, false, null),
  ('7b1c6b43-a4d1-5eda-9a44-60e2ef2c260c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', '(c) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SSGs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months serving in a Rail Advisor position or a position of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff (ASI 2S); Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course. Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course. Joint Operational Planning and Execution System (JOPES).
(e) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(f) Earned Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge
(g) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Railway Advisor.
(j) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor, ALC Instructor.
2. Highly qualified SSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in a position such as Railway Advisor.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded ALC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Rail Head Operations Group Training Course; Track Inspection Certification; Locomotive Engineer Certification; Locomotive Conductor Certification.
(e) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Railway Advisor.
(f) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor/Writer, ALC Instructor.
(d) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Decision Making, Problem Solving, General Cognitive Ability, Situational Awareness, Reasoning, Psychomotor Ability, Safety & Compliance, Management, Training and Developing Others, and General Communication.', '1898916a69ac548202be1a3ffcc4668ea79544fcb5b337a82a9cafd9e4875a50', 40, 41, '40', 196, null, null, false, null),
  ('ff36ecfd-8a63-5879-851d-e0837ab3d50e', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Continue pursuing higher-level civilian education opportunities, with a goal of completing an associate degree. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', '5ec759dcb05ee5524faaa48ce1b0a45df30386ec8bfc1d2dda7daae62e745ab2', 41, 41, '41', 197, null, null, false, null),
  ('e389f9be-1175-5bf5-a448-28e7c1418a04', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Functional training includes railroad track standards and maintenance training courses. Additional training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE) and/or Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP), and Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional; however important training includes BSNCOC, and the Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn promotion points for Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88U on ACT for more information.', '259f1dd1d617d4f5ce5685f27f0d8119ca4efe083dee4b16d12e7806911de056', 41, 42, '41', 198, null, null, false, null),
  ('eb6f707b-907a-5891-a5c0-58c541d908c2', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Recruiter, Drill Sergeant, SHARP, Career Counselor.', '0c060f6da6da29df10182940e89b34f469bc771cbf9fcd89ac6dedf0ee83f29f', 42, 42, '42', 199, null, null, false, null),
  ('a8d99a19-ad3d-5ded-a134-2511375e1722', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'In preparation for promotion to MSG, complete SLC. Attend Master Leader Course (MLC), if selected. Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education Course I (SEJPME I).', 'e7c418cd6c2daa6f9f0b6f1db2b499e7f1d5e7e664805d7d5e250afd81c32195', 42, 42, '42', 200, null, null, false, null),
  ('4c43861a-a9e6-55b5-9db6-1c9a40a14cf4', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Continue to seek out the leadership positions. NCOs who have served successfully and frequently in tough leadership positions are considered more competitive for promotion than those who have not.', 'bdf3dbd92895eb143d50cb1e990447a55e4039894e08ef4d9143099177356a5f', 42, 42, '42', 201, null, null, false, null),
  ('ebc55e7e-b9cd-5ee7-91ac-2234f67131ec', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', '(c) Promotion indicators. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified SFCs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in a Senior Rail Advisor position or a position of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff NCO (ASI 2S); Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Courses; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course. Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course. Joint Operational Planning and Execution System (JOPES).
(e) Become a member of the SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; recognized as NCO of the Quarter/Year; Instructor of the Year; Transportation Corps NCO of the Year.
(f) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(g) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Senior Rail Advisor.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor; ALC Instructor.
2. Highly qualified SFCs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in a position such as Senior Rail Advisor.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SLC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as Rail Head Operations Group Training Course; Track Inspection Certification; Locomotive Engineer Certification; Locomotive Conductor Certification.
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Senior Rail Advisor.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as AIT Instructor, ALC Instructor.
(d) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Decision Making, Management, Problem Solving, Multi-Domain Collaboration, Situational Awareness, Reasoning, Safety & Compliance, Training and Developing Others, and General Communication.', '39ddd2d9151485c86464ecd17c7aa5c1b08ffbc3813b13f01be391943bfcf9af', 42, 43, '42', 202, null, null, false, null),
  ('edad377e-cfcc-5789-a7fa-986207f7dc3c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Complete associate degree. The completion of an associate degree conveys initiative and potential. Begin pursuing a bachelor’s degree or other higher-level education opportunities. For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3.', 'be21889698c9bbb1d53f5bed3774e7dbc99499dcbaa8b018ee35de61ddcef137', 43, 43, '43', 203, null, null, false, null),
  ('8081af33-e087-506e-9937-4ee4bb24b1b3', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Functional training includes railroad track standards and maintenance training courses. Additional training includes TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’- Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE) and/or Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP), and Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional however important training includes BSNCOC, and the Support Operations Course. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88U on ACT for more information.', 'bcf8153df331f0649003a2ff95995ca285d4fadae594ad9654b5d5f35d445607', 43, 43, '43', 204, null, null, false, null),
  ('bc89bb36-42d5-5e04-9e14-ab91fa733208', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'Recruiter.', 'cc6632549b003c742a3719bae9c5146644bdf6ac4054b4a091a6c97d2c904537', 43, 43, '43', 205, null, null, false, null),
  ('30294157-e453-5c61-a4c2-4c4fb516ded0', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88U', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army career degrees', 'Chapter 19. Military occupational specialty 88U Railway Specialist (Reserve Component)', 'See SOCAD Army Degree Program.
(5) Master Sergeant/First Sergeant and Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major. See Chapter 25.', 'f946bd2819a57b16cd9c6df082bd8f42e0627f6191dab7a9b4445b87d6f5206b', 43, 43, '43', 206, null, null, false, null),
  ('d62afba4-d419-5da4-989e-ea6185778934', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Attend U.S. Army Sergeants Major Course (SMC), if selected. Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education I and II (SEJPME I and II).', 'c4b5f865812a7a4dcdaa3e1da93122bc9c558bbf4f11a19066ebec498925d4b6', 44, 44, '44', 207, null, null, false, null),
  ('ba7e8f77-a596-5621-9481-5ffb81f67948', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'The critical assignment for a Master Sergeant is First Sergeant, of which a minimum time of 24 months and up to 36 months rated time as a First Sergeant is recommended. While all First Sergeant opportunities are beneficial, positions in Security Force Assistance Brigades (SFAB) offer unique experiences and access to training and certifications not available in other assignments. In addition to gaining First Sergeant experience, 88Z MSGs should seek opportunities to serve in staff level positions at the brigade and above level.', 'ff67bd45706001eae3b0b4dd86d96375d6d9de08e618af8b4131a1a81b8668f1', 44, 44, '44', 208, null, null, false, null),
  ('83dcdabc-2659-5be1-b5be-741f27d555d2', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'First Sergeant, Transportation Supervisor, Senior Truckmaster, and Operations Sergeant.', '1609068be33e8e26c5215f434be3eeeedd669b42cae9c2939cbeabe281888795', 44, 44, '44', 209, null, null, false, null),
  ('60cee1a9-6151-50b1-bbd9-eecf72631635', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — Broadening assignments', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Key opportunities include SLC Chief Instructor, Instructor, Operations Sergeant (WHTA), Inspector General NCO, Detachment Sergeant, European Detachment NCOIC, Senior Talent Management NCO, and TC Quality Assurance Senior NCO.', '73ecf6040c14c012341515bf72ec313e769d309e37f0da64744a9baa5c223d1a', 44, 44, '44', 210, null, null, false, null),
  ('8a6b58f1-1f84-52b6-a142-8d38144bcab3', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', '(e) Promotion indicators. NCOs who have served successfully and frequently in challenging leadership positions are considered to be more competitive for promotion than those who have not. Along with evaluating exceptional performance through achievements, personal awards, recognition, and civilian education, consider the following to identify the most and highly qualified MSGs for the next higher grade:
1. Most qualified MSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following First Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, Senior Truckmaster, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and maintain consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded MLC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff (ASI 2S); Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Course; Master Driver Training (ASI M9); Support Operations Course; Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC-AIMS II (Functional User); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES); AMMO-62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Joint Operational Planning and Execution System (JOPES); Senior Transportation Operations Course.
(e) Attended other training, such as, Air Assault, Airborne, Security Forces Assistance Brigade (SFAB) Course, or Ranger School.
(f) Become a member of SGT Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; be recognized as Instructor of the Year, or as a Distinguished Member of the Regiment (DMOR).
(g) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Transportation Supervisor.
(i) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as SLC Chief Instructor, Instructor, Operations Sergeant (WHTA), Inspector General NCO; Detachment Sergeant, European Detachment NCOIC, Senior Talent Management NCO, and TC Quality Assurance Senior NCO.
2. Highly qualified MSGs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in one of the following positions First Sergeant, Operations Sergeant, Senior Truckmaster, or positions of greater responsibility.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded MLC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as MRT; SHARP; EOA; MFT.
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Transportation Supervisor.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as SLC Chief Instructor, Instructor, Operations Sergeant (WHTA), Inspector General NCO, Detachment Sergeant, European Detachmetn NCOIC, Senior Talent Management NCO, and TC Quality Assurance Senior NCO
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Management, Training and Developing Others, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Multi-Domain Collaboration, Reasoning, Communication, Sustains Climate & Morale, and Performance Management', '8ebcfc8b41580c84f6810596ac1fc1f06c69d52ba8cfb975e7388d9950a1680c', 44, 45, '44', 211, null, null, false, null),
  ('b0b33bff-5a8d-5d3a-aa85-bf8784a60e6f', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'For additional information on self-development, see Chapter 3. .', '003c6ecf65a3fcb5ed5dd47b4784b33209aa840fef014c6b292745c422426141', 45, 45, '45', 212, null, null, false, null),
  ('ee03cd69-1bbc-5de5-a36f-3b84389f05df', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Additional training includes Senior Transportation Operations Course (STOC), TC-AIMS II, (Transportation Coordinators’-Automated Information for Movements System II) Integrated Data Environment (IDE) and/or Global Transportation Network (GTN) Convergence (IGC), ICODES, Joint Aircraft Load Planning, Joint Container Management Course, and Military Standard Transportation and Movement Procedures (MILSTAMP). Other training includes Technical TRANS of HAZMAT (CERT). Other nonfunctional training includes BSNCOC, Support Operations Course, How the Army Runs Course, and JOPES. Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88Z on ACT for more information.', 'e9bc1f0cdf09f159fe19ef236fc5830f5455e90b87dfbafeb28be14dcc91b6cd', 45, 45, '45', 213, null, null, false, null),
  ('5f9e5cf6-3352-582a-9bf8-b3486c352f08', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant and First Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'White House Transportation Agency (WHTA) Operations Sergeant. WHTA provides 24-hour transportation and cargo support services and assists with worldwide transportation support for presidential motorcades and presidential travel as directed by the White House Military Office (WHMO). Soldiers assigned to WHTA could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. Additional special assignments include Senior Career Advisor (HRC), Inspector General NCO, NATO, Observer Controller/Trainer, Chief Instructor SLC Branch, and positions within United States Army JFK Special Warfare Center and School (USAJFKSWCS), 160th Special Operations Aviation Regiment (SOAR), and Special Mission Units (SMU). These positions should be considered career enhancing assignments.', '1310b57cb5b8d162708926a4cf5d9c2036564db13e8477734b3458b16c472791', 45, 45, '45', 214, null, null, false, null),
  ('ff43ce6c-2891-5e73-8be1-687053394622', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major and Command Sergeant Major — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Executive Leader Course (ELC). Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education I and II (SEJPME I and II).', '657bb02ea8d4c68bfc38507e027238c448177cb1fe77c819c7796e1e53b2d334', 45, 45, '45', 215, null, null, false, null),
  ('80a227f7-2add-53a5-81fe-9c1962bf2447', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major and Command Sergeant Major — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'SGMs should pursue leadership positions as the Command Sergeant Major at the Battalion and Brigade level.', '1a45fc377339e0834abebe31c7f4f78bc70e5d5374e07de02095a258561d319a', 45, 45, '45', 216, null, null, false, null),
  ('e9d10a61-c6b3-588c-b3ae-2e07c4629a4b', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major and Command Sergeant Major — Career Development assignments', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Command Sergeant Major, SDDC Battalion Sergeant Major, Senior Enlisted Advisor, Operations Sergeant Major, Senior Transportation Supervisor, Division or Corps Transportation Sergeant Major.', '78ce42c8e6e32f2c8d4eff7d0d116d9489f7d85f9d165492d46678b825dfcb45', 46, 46, '46', 217, null, null, false, null),
  ('a454a8b2-b007-504b-b502-53c94913f7de', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major and Command Sergeant Major — Broadening Assignment', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Key opportunities include Instructor, Logistics Proponent NCO, Senior Career Management NCO, Inspector General SGM, Senior Instructor (MTOC SGM), Senior Enlisted Advisor (WHTA).', '9ef0333bdb66eca194acd2a5d12eaf06fee25ef3b0fd70e4e9ae1975041865e8', 46, 46, '46', 218, null, null, false, null),
  ('91ce8713-3127-5682-b294-503124abe5c6', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major and Command Sergeant Major — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', '(e) Promotion indicators.
1. Most qualified SGM/CSMs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance for 24 months in one of the following positions Command Sergeant Major; Battalion Sergeant Major, Senior Enlisted Advisor.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SMC course standards (Distinguished Honor/Honor Graduate) or received an award for Leadership.
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended Battle Staff (ASI 2S); Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course; Master Resiliency Trainer (MRT) Course; Master Driver Trainer (ASI M9); Support Operations Course; Senior Transportation Operations Course; Operational Contracting Support (ASI 3C); Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL) Course; Victim Advocate (VA) Course; Unit Movement Officer Deployment Planning Course (UMODPC); TC- AIMS II (Functional User); Integrated Computerized Deployment System (ICODES); AMMO- 62 Technical Transportation of Hazmat Course; Joint Operational Planning and execution Systems (JOPES).
(e) Become a member of the Sergeant Audie Murphy/Sergeant Morales Club; honored as a Distinguished Member of the Regiment (DMOR).
(f) Earned the Instructor Badge or Expert Soldier Badge.
(g) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Senior Transportation Supervisor, Operations Sergeant Major, Division or Corps Transportation Sergeant Major.
(h) Demonstrated exceptional duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Instructor, Logistics Proponent NCO, Senior Career Management NCO, Inspector General SGM, Senior Instructor (MTOC SGM), Senior Enlisted Advisor (WHTA).
2. Highly qualified SGM/CSMs will have demonstrated any combination of the following:
(a) Successfully served 12-18 months in positions such as Command Sergeant Major, Battalion Sergeant Major, Senior Enlisted Advisor.
(b) Maintained high physical fitness standards and consistent compliance with height and weight standards.
(c) Exceeded SMC course standards (Commandant’s List).
(d) Consistently pursued military education and attended courses such as MRT; SHARP; EOL; MFT.
(e) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Career Developmental positions such as Senior Transportation Supervisor, Operations Sergeant Major, Division or Corps Transportation Sergeant Major.
(f) Demonstrated successful duty performance while assigned in Broadening Assignments such as Instructor, Logistics Proponent NCO, Senior Career Management NCO, Inspector General SGM, Senior Instructor (MTOC SGM), Senior Enlisted Advisor (WHTA).
(f) Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors: Leadership, Management, Training and Developing Others, Decision Making, Problem Solving, Multi-Domain Collaboration, Reasoning, Communication, Sustains Climate & Morale, and Performance Management', '112469182187590df3e42113786561ac2624dbeb7e41a91b304da636948dd7f4', 46, 46, '46', 219, null, null, false, null),
  ('c0f6b6ca-fc20-5467-adfc-7c067067f07c', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major and Command Sergeant Major — Self-development', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Although not a requirement for promotion to Sergeant Major, it is recommended for Sergeant Majors to complete a bachelor’s degree. The Sergeant Major should enroll in a graduate program after completion of a bachelor’s degree.', 'a6b8250258ca7455e125e18d0b410f55e2c762fcb6891aa3cb67f33cd6a04c88', 47, 47, '47', 220, null, null, false, null),
  ('13f60168-a500-5731-90d4-2c57dc4aa591', '6bc66bce-708a-518c-a0f3-be024e3e2b44', 'Army', 'enlisted', '88Z', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major and Command Sergeant Major — Additional training', 'Chapter 21. Military occupational specialty 88Z Transportation Senior Sergeant', 'Soldiers may also earn Technical Certifications; a list of certifications is available on the ArmyIgnitEd website. See Professional Development Model (PDM) for 88Z on ACT. Special assignments. Senior Career Management Sergeant Major. Serves as the Proponent Sergeant Major responsible for managing personnel Proponency issues for all TC enlisted Soldiers; formulates plans, policies, and programs pertaining to force structure, acquisition, training, distribution, sustainment, deployment, and separation of enlisted Soldiers for the Chief of Transportation (COT); coordinates with HQDA and major commands to achieve proponent objectives; serves as enlisted advisor to the Director, Office of the Chief of Transportation (OCOT), Regimental Command Sergeant Major and the Chief of Transportation.
1. Assistant Inspector General Sergeant Major, (HQ, SDDC). Fact finders who use training, inspections, staff and/or unit assist visits, as well as investigation as their primary tool to assist leadership, staff, or the field.
2. SMC SGL, SMC instructor/writer. The Regiment recommends favorable consideration to those who serve or have served in the aforementioned positions 12 months or longer and performed duties in an exemplary manner.
3. The White House Transportation Agency (WHTA). WHTA provides 24-hour transportation and cargo support services to the First Family, White House staff, and official visitors of the First Family in the Washington DC area; assists with worldwide transportation support for presidential motorcades and presidential travel as directed by the White House Military Office (WHMO); supervises and assists with the transportation of Presidential gift trunks. NCOs assigned to these commands could have longer than normal utilization tours due to mission and training requirements. These positions should be considered as career enhancing assignments.
(g) Army career degrees. See SOCAD Army Degree Program.', '262395a25d89d5301a3aa0d5087338737bea58ad0019d65acd8dbfdf83fb5575', 47, 47, '47', 221, null, null, false, null);
